WEBVTT

00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,400
What other kinds of foods would be beneficial from an epigenetic point of view?

00:00:05,360 --> 00:00:07,840
Beneficial for cancer patients? Yes.

00:00:09,120 --> 00:00:14,400
Well, more so what foods are probably best to stay away from a genetic point of view.

00:00:15,120 --> 00:00:21,280
And certainly with any cancer, you're trying to limit growth. So then you look at what foods

00:00:21,280 --> 00:00:27,520
stimulate growth pathways, metabolic pathways, and the first one that you should probably consider

00:00:27,920 --> 00:00:35,680
dairy products. So dairy, I wouldn't say dairy is necessarily a cause of cancer, per se, but it

00:00:35,680 --> 00:00:44,400
certainly is a stimulant to growth factors. You try to explain it to people, what is dairy for

00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:53,280
its milk for a baby for a 60 pound cow to grow up to be a 1200 pound cow? We certainly don't want to

00:00:53,280 --> 00:00:58,240
be adding growth factors. And I show it in videos, different men of the metabolic pathways to

00:00:58,240 --> 00:01:02,800
get them to understand that stimulates the caross pathway, which is a growth pathway.

00:01:03,440 --> 00:01:10,640
To get them to understand the technical side of that, but staying away from things that will stimulate

00:01:10,640 --> 00:01:18,000
growth of the cancer. So then we talk about from a dietary standpoint, cancer needs a fuel source.

00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:25,200
So whereas dairy is not necessarily a fuel source, it's a growth stimulator. But what is a

00:01:25,200 --> 00:01:30,560
fuel source of a cancer? It could be fed mainly directly through the pathway called glycolysis,

00:01:30,560 --> 00:01:37,600
which is how we break down glucose. So sugar should probably be something that all cancer patients

00:01:37,600 --> 00:01:45,760
should refrain from. But there are certain people that their cancer is stimulated completely

00:01:45,840 --> 00:01:51,760
off glycolysis, or that's the main source of fuel we could say. And then there's other people that

00:01:51,760 --> 00:01:58,720
their cancer currently is fueled off of amino acid, gobbling up amino acids, and that is the

00:01:58,720 --> 00:02:08,400
fuel source, lysine and methionate and glutamine. So those people should limit animal products

00:02:08,400 --> 00:02:14,240
like meat. That should be the main thing that they limit, that they should be eating a bunch of

00:02:14,480 --> 00:02:23,600
carbohydrates, but they really have to limit protein sources. And typically it's animal protein sources

00:02:23,600 --> 00:02:31,680
what we found. So it can vary. Some people really should be eating some animal proteins, and some

00:02:31,680 --> 00:02:36,800
people should not be eating any animal proteins. Probably every cancer across the board should stay

00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:42,720
away from dairy. Every cancer across the board should stay away from glucose, sugar, sucrose,

00:02:43,280 --> 00:02:49,120
has really no nutritional value. But some people don't need to stay away from fruit,

00:02:50,240 --> 00:02:57,040
and vegetable juicy, which could be high in glucose breakdown, but has all these other

00:02:57,040 --> 00:03:01,600
nutritional values. And if their cancer isn't fed directly through glycolysis, that's where

00:03:01,600 --> 00:03:09,760
juicy can be very beneficial for those people. So it does vary from person to person, not so much

00:03:09,760 --> 00:03:14,640
cancer to cancer, but person to person, the fuel source of that cancer.

00:03:14,640 --> 00:03:20,240
Can you determine this through the DNA testing? You could get hints through the DNA testing, yes.

00:03:21,600 --> 00:03:32,720
Dr. Godzilla and Dr. William Kelly did question-air testing, metabolic testing they called it.

00:03:33,600 --> 00:03:42,560
We do kinesiology testing as well to help determine that. A person not having any access to any of

00:03:42,560 --> 00:03:48,640
those things could look at how they feel after they eat those things. Or if I juice it,

00:03:48,640 --> 00:03:55,680
I don't feel as well when I'm juicing. Or if I don't eat some meat, I don't feel well at all.

00:03:55,680 --> 00:04:02,240
Those are some hints that you could gather for what is possibly causing your cancer growth.

00:04:02,320 --> 00:04:07,760
Certainly, if you have a tumor that's visible and palpable, you can tell sometimes when

00:04:08,480 --> 00:04:14,880
what you're eating is adverse to the cancer. So there's different ways that you can tell

00:04:14,880 --> 00:04:22,080
what's what's currently feeding your cancer. But you want to try to cut off that pathway as much as possible.

